        "subtitle": "Tip it all in and walk away",
        "description": "Pineapple, pie filling, dry cake mix and butter, layered in a tin without stirring anything. It has no business working and it works every single time.",
        "instructions": [
          "Spread the pineapple over the bottom of a 9X13 pan.",
          "Cover it with the pie filling, right to the corners.",
          "Tip the dry cake mix over the top in an even layer. Don't stir it in — the whole trick is that the layers stay separate.",
          "Cut the butter into small pieces and dot them evenly over the cake mix. Anywhere you miss will stay powdery, so be thorough about it.",
          "Bake at 350 for 1 hour, until the top is golden and the fruit is bubbling up at the edges.",
          "Serve it old school with Cool Whip, or with fresh whipped cream if you'd rather."
        ]
